How Workers Queue Up in Front of the Workplace
You can set how arriving Workers, who cannot step onto the Workplace, wait in the queue in front of it.
Remarks
Plant Simulation queues these Workers, without using additional FootPaths, in the queue at their waiting
position. The waiting position is determined according to the position in the Forward Blocking List of
the Workplace. Let's say the Worker is located at the third position in the Forward Blocking List, then he
also waits at the third place in the queue.
The waiting position is the position at which the Worker waits until it is his turn to step onto the
Workplace. The waiting position depends on his position in the Forward Blocking List and the distance
between the Workers in the queue. Once a waiting Worker moves up in the Forward Blocking List, he also
moves up in the queue.
In new models Plant Simulation visualizes the queue on the MU Animation Path named Queue of the
Workplace. If the queue is longer than the pre-defined MU Animation Path, Plant Simulation elongates it
toward the end of the queue.
You can set the Distance between the Workers in the queue on the animation path.
How Workers Queue Up in Front of the Workplace
11-2976 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If you do not want the Worker to walk to the Workplace, but to the end of the MU Animation Path, select
Walk Along the Animation Path of the Queue.
After the Worker has reached the end of the MU Animation Path, Plant Simulation computes the direct
way to the waiting position or to the Workplace respectively.
Working with the Worker Queue
• If the Worker is to Model Workers Who Walk to the End of the Queue, the end of the animation path
has to be positioned at the same height (Z-position) as the Workplace.
If this is not the case, Plant Simulation might not be able to compute a route to the end of the animation
path.
Once the Worker arrived at the end of the animation path and provided the Workplace is still available
while computing the route, Plant Simulation sets the Workplace as the target, even if other Workers
might already be on their way to the Workplace on the animation path.
If the Worker arrives at a Workplace or at a waiting position that is occupied, Plant Simulation moves
him directly to the correct waiting position.
If the end of the animation path is located after the actual waiting position, the Worker walks along the
animation path to this waiting position.
If the queue is longer, so that the Worker stands in the queue once he has reached the end of the
animation path, he walks through the already waiting Workers to his waiting position.
• Activating Walk Along the Animation Path of the Queue and reaching the waiting position or the
Workplace via a Footpath is relevant for the simulation as the times during which the Worker is on his
way do change.
Plant Simulation does not use up any time for reaching the waiting position if the Worker walks directly
to the Workplace. Plant Simulation then shows him at the respective waiting position in the queue.
The same is true when the Worker moves up within the queue as these movements are executed by the
respective animation of the Worker.
