Tab Times [Workplace]
Define Times as described under the Tab Times.
The tab Times provides these settings:
Loading Time [Workplace]
Unloading Time [Workplace]
Recovery Time [Workplace]
Select a distribution from the drop-down list and type the values that this distribution requires into the
text box. Plant Simulation shows the parameters along the upper border of the tab. You can also select a
constant time (Const).
You can set the type of the distribution and a complete set of parameters with the method
setTypeAndAttr [SimTalk].
Tab Times
11-2994 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Loading Time [Workplace]
Select a distribution, and type the values which that distribution requires into the text box. Plant
Simulation shows these values along the upper border of the tab. You can also type in a constant time
(Const).
Remarks
You can set the type of the distribution and a complete set of parameters with the method
setTypeAndAttr [SimTalk].
If you select the Formula distribution, you can type in a numeric expression or the name of a Method.
You can use the anonymous identifier @ to access the part for which the specified time applies. The
anonymous identifier ? points to the Workplace. You can access the Worker with ?.Cont.
Loading Time
The Loading Time is the time it takes the Worker for picking up a single part at a station. After the
Loading Time has elapsed, the Worker waits for the Maximum Dwell Time to pass if he still has carrying
capacity. If not, he immediately carries the part to the target station and places it there. If the Worker is to
load more than one part, the Maximum Dwell Time should at least be as long the carrying capacity times
the Loading Time.
The part is booked on the Worker while he picks it up. The processing station is locked until the Loading
Time has elapsed.
Note
The entrance of the Workplace is closed while its Loading Time is running as the Worker functions with
reservations for the Workplace.
Behavior During Interruptions of the Worker
Plant Simulation extends the Loading Time by failure times of the Worker. The processing station
remains locked during the failure.
If the Worker pauses during the Loading Time, Plant Simulation cancels the Loading Time and considers
it as completely elapsed. This means that the Worker carries at least one part to the WorkerPool.
If the shift ends during the Loading Time, Plant Simulation cancels the Loading Time and considers it as
completely elapsed. This means that the Worker carries at least one part to the parts buffer.
Loading Time [Workplace]
Plant Simulation Help 11-2995
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Behavior During Interruptions of the Processing Station
Failures of the processing station do not affect loading the part by the Worker. The part is already located
at the Worker and loading takes place during the failure.
The same applies for processing stations which are stopped, paused, or unplanned.
SimTalk
LoadingTime [SimTalk] - Workplace
LoadingTime [SimTalk] - Workplace.Type [SimTalk] - distribution parameter
See also
Formula [distribution]
Loading Time [Workplace]
11-2996 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Unloading Time [Workplace]
Select a distribution, and type the values which that distribution requires into the text box. Plant
Simulation shows these values along the upper border of the tab. You can also type in a constant time
(Const).
Remarks
You can set the type of the distribution and a complete set of parameters with the method
setTypeAndAttr [SimTalk].
If you select the Formula distribution, you can type in a numeric expression or the name of a Method.
You can use the anonymous identifier @ to access the part for which the specified time applies. The
anonymous identifier ? points to the Workplace. You can access the Worker with ?.Cont.
Unloading Time
The Unloading Time is the time it takes the Worker for placing the part he picked up at another station
onto the target station. If he is to unload several parts, the Unloading Time accrues for each part.
The part is booked on the Worker while he places it on the target station. The target processing station is
locked until the Unloading Time has elapsed.
Behavior During Interruptions of the Worker
Plant Simulation extends the Unloading Time by failure times of the Worker. The target processing
station remains locked during the failure.
If the Worker pauses during the Unloading Time, Plant Simulation cancels the unloading time. The
target processing station does not remain locked, and the Worker takes the parts to the WorkerPool with
him. After the pause is over, unloading starts anew.
If the shift ends during the Unloading Time, Plant Simulation cancels the Unloading Time and the
Worker carries the part to the parts buffer. The target processing station does not remain locked.
Behavior During Interruptions of the Processing Station Through a Failure, Pause, etc.
The Worker only starts unloading when the target processing station can take on the part for processing. If
this is not the case, Plant Simulation enters the part to be unloaded into the Forward Blocking List. The
Unloading Time starts after the interruption is over.
Unloading Time [Workplace]
Plant Simulation Help 11-2997
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The Worker continues unloading the part when the target processing station is being interrupted during
the Unloading Time. Plant Simulation also enters the part to be unloaded into Forward Blocking List if
the target processing station cannot accept a part at the time of the actual unloading process (after the
unloading time has elapsed). The part stays with the Worker. After the interruption has been removed, the
Worker deposits the part onto the target processing station without any time delay.
SimTalk
UnloadingTime [SimTalk] - Workplace
UnloadingTime [SimTalk] - Workplace.Type [SimTalk] - distribution parameter
See also
Formula [distribution]
Unloading Time [Workplace]
11-2998 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Recovery Time [Workplace]
Select a distribution, and type in the values which that distribution requires into the text box. Plant
Simulation shows these values along the upper border of the tab. You can also type in a constant time
(Const).
Remarks
The predefined Recovery Time in the class of the Workplace prevents that a Worker steps onto the
Workplace while the Worker, who is already located on it, has not left it all the way.
Note
You can only define the Recovery Time for a Workplace that has a Capacity of 1. The Recovery Time
starts once a Worker leaves the Workplace.
Note
The Recovery Time will not take effect, if you set the Workplace as the Home Location of a Worker and
if the Worker wants to step onto this Home Location/Workplace.
You can set the type of the distribution and a complete set of parameters with the method
setTypeAndAttr [SimTalk].
If you select the Formula distribution, you can type in a numeric expression or the name of a Method.
You can use the anonymous identifier @ to access the part for which the specified time applies. The
anonymous identifier ? points to the Workplace. You can access the Worker with ?.Cont.
